      "raw_response": "ANSWER: SUPPORTED\n\nSource: Full text of the article \"N348I in the Connection Domain of HIV-1 Reverse Transcriptase Confers Zidovudine and Nevirapine Resistance\" by the British Columbia Centre for Excellence in HIV/AIDS and other associated researchers. Confidence level: High. The study directly supports the claim that N348I mutations confer resistance to zidovudine and nevirapine. The researchers observed a significant increase in the prevalence of N348I in treatment-experienced patients and found that it was associated with increased viral load and decreased susceptibility to the drugs mentioned. The mutation's effects on zidovudine susceptibility were also demonstrated in vitro with recombinant RT containing N348I.",
